       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 9,000 mg/day is a toxic dose. It is well into the range where hepatotoxicity is expected, and I know of no clinical indication that justifies it. You also haven't given a rationale. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day).\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or your order-entry override pathway.** If you believe there's an unusual indication, a pharmacist should review it. That route also gives you a documented second check.\n- **Look at other options if pain or fever control is the goal.** Scheduled NSAIDs or other multimodal analgesia could work, depending on the patient.\n\nIf the dose was a slip, such as 3,000 mg/day total, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
